# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/cheat_probe.script - VERIFY a third-party cheat table, do not trust it.
#
# Created 2026-10-03 (T107). The cheat table is third-party community content
# and is treated here as a SET OF HYPOTHESES ABOUT ADDRESSES, to be checked
# against this project's own measurements. Nothing in this script is enabled in
# any shipped build; it is a probe and it is never run by a gate.
#
# WHAT IS BEING TESTED, and why each poke is byte-for-byte as published:
#
#   7E0B53A0 + 7E0B540F  "year 4000"  -> $0FA0 = 4000
#     Applied as the two 8-bit writes the published pair actually is:
#       poke 0B53 A0      -> $A0 to $0B53
#       poke 0B54 0F      -> $0F to $0B54
#     Little-endian, so the 16-bit word at $0B53 becomes $0FA0. We have measured
#     $0B53 as the 16-bit absolute year (1900 = $076C), from the inside.
#
#   7E0BA520 + 7E0BA64E  "population 20000" -> $4E20 = 20000
#       poke 0BA5 20      -> $20 to $0BA5
#       poke 0BA6 4E      -> $4E to $0BA6
#     We have measured $0BA5 as a 16-bit field that is 0 in every sample of both
#     builds. NOTE the tension and do not resolve it here: we also measure
#     $0B9D = $4E20 = 20000, the SAME value, and we call THAT one funds. A cheat
#     claiming "population = 20000" for an address that reads 0 is exactly the
#     entry whose LABEL needs checking, not its arithmetic.
#
#   7E03F501 .. 7E03F50A  ten codes, values $01..$0A all to the SAME address.
#     Under the plaintext reading this is one 8-bit selector field written with
#     ten different values - i.e. a building-type picker, not "bank 3".
#     Probed here as poke 0 03F5 0A (the tenth), the largest, to see whether the
#     field exists at all.
#
#   7E0BF9EB  "start with 49000". 49000 = $BF68. The published code writes $EB to
#     $0BF9. $BF68 is not what that produces, and $0BF9 is not an address we have
#     measured. Probed anyway: if $0BF9 is a real field it will have a value here.
#
#   C28A-AD61 / E28A-AD61  write $61 to $8AAD. $8AAD is INSIDE the region the
#     $03C87x runaway zero-fill overwrote ($6B00..$F8F3), so this probe also
#     records what our own emulator left there.
#
# Each poke is separated by `wait` so the WRAM dumps bracket them one at a time.
# SNESRECOMP_WRAM_DUMP_AT takes the frame list; run with the values in the commit
# body. Host-only nothing: this is Deck-native.
#
# NOT DELIVERABLE, NOT A GATE, NOT A FEATURE. If any of this ever makes
# `make clock` pass, that is a DIAGNOSTIC and it is recorded as one - the gate
# requires the clock to advance with no cheats and no pokes. See
# docs/DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md Rule 0 and docs/CHEAT_CODES.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

wait 250
press start 5
wait 120
press down 5
wait 120
press b 5
wait 120
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
press b 5
wait 90
wait 300
press left 5
wait 150
press down 5
wait 90
mouseclick right 6
wait 200
press down 5
wait 90
mouseclick right 6
wait 200
press down 5
wait 90
mouseclick right 6
wait 200
press down 5
wait 90
mouseclick right 6
wait 200
wait 400

# ---- the probe proper ------------------------------------------------------
# The city is live and settled by here. Pokes, one per field, spaced.
wait 200
poke 0B53 A0
wait 120
poke 0B54 0F
wait 120
poke 0BA5 20
wait 120
poke 0BA6 4E
wait 120
poke 0BF9 EB
wait 120
poke 8AAD 61
wait 120
poke 03F5 0A
wait 120
wait 600
